set.body:
Close the non-algorithmic migration surface before legacy deletion.

Scope:
- multiblock partitions and cross-projections;
- RowGeometry bridges and whitening-derived relations;
- neuroimaging plan/spec boundaries and typed estimator selection;
- fit/result bundles, projection/export adapters, and serialization hooks;
- documentation and examples that construct legacy MvMetric, MvMap, DualityDiagram, or GenPca objects.

Preserve module acyclicity. Plans describe semantic programs and capabilities; they do not become solver engines. Fit artifacts expose FunctionalFrame, derived scores/axes/operators, result equivalence, diagnostics, and provenance.

Acceptance:
- all affected shared JVM/JS suites pass;
- plan serialization and fit lifting have round-trip tests;
- row-geometry conversions carry explicit evidence and tolerance;
- repository search shows no unowned legacy consumer outside compatibility adapters;
- shared dependency scan remains clean.
